  "confirmed": [
    "NoteSingleBase.MoveState invokes NoteManager.GetAdjustMusicPos and only enters judgement after the adjusted score position reaches the note absolute position.",
    "When InGameCalculatedData.get_IsAutoPlay is true, that crossing dispatches the note's forcePerfect virtual method in the same MoveState update.",
    "NoteSingleBase.forcePerfect submits NoteResultType.Perfect (4).",
    "JudgementAdjustValueB is restricted to -5 through 5 by the recovered settings UI, and each unit moves the adjusted score position by one tempo-aware 1/60-second step.",
    "Under the explicit B=0 model, the portable 30 Hz particle peak range does not overlap the formal-play range."
  ],
  "inference": [
    "B=4 is the closest discrete setting in the recovered range: it moves the portable median to within 1.736498 ms of the formal-play median and places the portable range inside the formal-play range.",
    "A formal-play value of B=4 could therefore explain the previously measured phase mismatch without requiring a four-frame particle lifecycle correction."
  ],
  "unresolved": [
    "The JudgementAdjustValueB value active during the formal recording has not been captured from LiveCoreSettings, so B=4 is not a confirmed runtime fact.",
    "This scalar phase model does not establish Unity PlayerLoop, random-stream, ParticleSystem lifecycle, or GPU pixel parity.",
    "Long and Slide Auto Live forcePerfect state paths require their own type-specific integration rather than inheriting the NoteSingleBase model wholesale."
  ],
